      "blind_answer": 2,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "HCHO has no electron-releasing alkyl groups and the least steric hindrance, so its carbonyl carbon is the most electrophilic and accessible."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u17_t08_2",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
        3
      ],
      "blind_answer": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "-NO2 withdraws electrons and raises carbonyl electrophilicity. -CH3 donates weakly (+I/hyperconjugation). -OCH3 donates strongly (+R). Order: P > B > T > M."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u17_t08_3",
      "published": true,
