      ],
      "blind_answer": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "In benzaldehyde the ring conjugates with C=O and donates electron density by resonance, lowering the electrophilicity of the carbonyl carbon. Option 3 is wrong (α-H is irrelevant to nucleophilic attack) and option 4 is wrong (propanal has only one alkyl group on the carbonyl carbon)."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u17_t08_4",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
